<page>
    <paragraphs>
        <title>Applications of Functions</title>
        
        <p>
            Whenever we have an application problem, like the ones we've solved before, we can often phrase the question in terms of a function.
        </p>

        <example workspace="3in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Assume that you are trying to build a rectangular garden bed alongside a house. You have 40 feet of fencing to use to put along the three sides of the garden bed (you don't need to fence the side that is against the house). Write a function for the area of the garden bed in terms of the length of the bed (the side parallel to the house).
                </p>
            </statement>
        <solution component="a">
            <p>
                Test
            </p>
        </solution>
        </example>
        
    </paragraphs>
</page>

<page>
    <paragraphs>
        <title>Piecewise Functions</title>
        <p component="b" workspace="2in">
            It is sometimes the case that the formula of a function changes depending on the input. The most direct example of this is tax brackets.
        </p>
        <p component="a">
            It is sometimes the case that the formula of a function changes depending on the input. The most direct example of this is tax brackets. Rate changes, pay it on the money over a certain threshold. Also, bulk purchases at a store.
        </p>

        <p component="b" workspace="2in">
            We have a specific way of writing out a piecewise function to display the appropriate information.
        </p>
        <p component="a">
            We have a specific way of writing out a piecewise function to display the appropriate information. cases brace, domain part, formula part.
        </p>
    </paragraphs>
</page>
<page>
    <example>
        <introduction>
            <p>
                Consider the function <m>f(x)</m> defined below
                <md>
                    f(x) = \begin{cases}
                        2x+4 \amp x &lt; -2 \\
                        3 \amp -2 \leq x \leq 1\\
                        4-x \amp x &gt; 1
                    \end{cases}
                </md>.
            </p>
        </introduction>
            <task workspace="2in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Evaluate <m>f(-4)</m>, <m>f(0)</m>, <m>f(-2)</m>, <m>f(3)</m>, and <m>f(5)</m>.
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Sketch a graph of <m>f(x)</m>.
                    </p>
<image component="b" width="60%">
  <prefigure xmlns="https://prefigure.org"
             label="fcns-piecewise-example-one-blank">
    <xi:include href="../../prefigure/blank-axes-6-6.xml" />
  </prefigure>
</image>
                </statement>
                <solution component="a">
                        <image component="a" width="60%">
  <prefigure xmlns="https://prefigure.org"
             label="fcns-piecewise-example-one">
    <xi:include href="../../prefigure/fcns-piecewise-example-one.xml" />
  </prefigure>
</image>
                </solution>
            </task>
    </example>
    
</page>

<page>
